# CODEOWNERS — automatic review requests on pull requests
#
# Syntax:  <pattern>  <@owner1> <@owner2> ...
# A matching PR triggers a review request from the listed owners before merge.
# More specific rules (lower down) override broader rules above.
#
# Placeholder owners: replace @HamUniversal, @HamUniversal, and
# @HamUniversal with real GitHub handles before pushing.
# - @HamUniversal       : the sole maintainer / repo admin
# - @HamUniversal    : a team or user responsible for security review
#                              (create as a GitHub team, or use a single handle)
# - @HamUniversal : broader group for docs, content, i18n
#
# IMPORTANT: CODEOWNERS has no effect until these placeholders are real handles
# AND the file is on the default branch (main). Update both sides together.

# ============================================================================
# 1. SECURITY-SENSITIVE PATHS  — require security-team approval
# ============================================================================

# Secrets, environment config, and anything that touches API keys.
# config.js is gitignored in normal use (config.example.js is the template),
# but if it ever appears in a PR, it MUST be reviewed.
config.js                               @HamUniversal
config.example.js                       @HamUniversal
*.env                                   @HamUniversal
.env.*                                  @HamUniversal
**/secrets/**                           @HamUniversal

# Deployment credentials, hosting config, DNS, redirects.
netlify.toml                            @HamUniversal
vercel.json                             @HamUniversal
_redirects                              @HamUniversal
_dnslink                                @HamUniversal

# GitHub Actions workflows and release automation — supply-chain risk.
.github/                                @HamUniversal
.github/workflows/                      @HamUniversal
.github/actions/                        @HamUniversal

# Optional Node.js backend: email capture, fulfilment, API endpoints.
server.js                               @HamUniversal
package.json                            @HamUniversal
package-lock.json                       @HamUniversal

# ============================================================================
# 2. BACKEND & INTEGRATION LOGIC  — require maintainer approval
# ============================================================================

serve.py                                @HamUniversal
build.py                                @HamUniversal
pack.py                                 @HamUniversal
pack_now.py                             @HamUniversal
test_backend.py                         @HamUniversal

# ============================================================================
# 3. CONTENT & DOCUMENTATION  — broader review
# ============================================================================

*.md                                    @HamUniversal
docs/                                   @HamUniversal
LAUNCH.txt                              @HamUniversal
DELIVERABLES.txt                        @HamUniversal

# The actual site (HTML/CSS/JS) — content changes reviewed by maintainers.
index.html                              @HamUniversal
updated.html                            @HamUniversal
source-original.html                    @HamUniversal
js/                                     @HamUniversal
css/                                    @HamUniversal
assets/                                 @HamUniversal

# ============================================================================
# 4. EVERYTHING ELSE  — falls through to the repo owner
# ============================================================================

*                                       @HamUniversal
